damentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Idaho remains one of the most Republican states in the country, and the 2028 presidential race there opens with no state polls, no expert ratings, and no meaningful fundraising signals to test that standing. The contest is open with the incumbent president term-limited, so neither side gains an incumbency edge.\n\nNational coverage in 2026 described the president as underwater in 47 states, but Idaho appears to sit among the handful of states where his standing holds, reinforcing the state's Republican baseline. With no evidence of a competitive campaign, the forecast stays tied to Idaho's strong partisan lean, leaving Democrats only a slim chance of an upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0246, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0537, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0476, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0546, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0466, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0509, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0538, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -17.0}]}